{:edb/db-before-t 964 :edb/db-after-t 965 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534277 50 #inst "2026-10-11T18:31:02.121Z" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186115070 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](images/40/406033f059dc4438ea55d43d2bd00b3b79bb99365a2e4846c995f4a447acfd82.svg)\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186115070 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](images/a5/a50d551e5d8abe8d9ae48778b195c382bbbf96f6fc5083c41b67642e99deffda.png)\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534277 17592186045417 false] [17592186115070 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](images/48/48c423256fbdc0d7e4f6ff716fb449efe6f98bdf57ba90353bcced930ea4ed17.png)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/81/81b7626ac30b06c5eeb10be274dd93476a86dce5fe3053722d96e16b78d7f165.png)\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-5y \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-5y \\\\ y \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534277 17592186045417 false] [17592186115070 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](images/be/bed2784d17ee63b805917b492052daa7ef079c1682bbc78468eb10f314a92b1f.svg)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/91/91175ab97472067cd14ffff740bb3a98718436f1e94de7a4a6d7fdfb1b35b81f.svg)\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-5y \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-5y \\\\ y \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186115071 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](images/6f/6fa4508463b059ce8ef9a5cfa720de9463e41ecdbfb16f4460870bb6fce444bc.svg)\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n![](images/21/215ff061dc7584055bf607f48d0048cb6bde4dcb1ed028fbf4c3a4bd47d89c25.svg)\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186115071 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](images/f4/f4478e5828da7c79a47bf3ca212ed15357befe7b0b208c78beb0895b445272c9.png)\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n![](images/cf/cfea36ae2b5cb5d8715480c1e0ee0b5ba06cf39d0c2032eb6e9b9078bf8c5bde.png)\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" 13194139534277 17592186045417 false] [17592186115124 1071 "Given the system\n![](images/0e/0e89fc57b6af2ddf2a71246dbadc7feb8425d1e1e0ab8f988e7e8ad97d22cff7.svg)\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n\n- The system has no solution\n\n- The system is consistent independent" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186115124 1071 "Given the system\n![](images/42/427c19efbebba6bfe2dc36bccd852d7a1f5e0ec97dc46c00043d019807e86ec2.png)\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n\n- The system has no solution\n\n- The system is consistent independent" 13194139534277 17592186045417 false] [17592186115124 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](images/3e/3e3e8adb0d6e13f7d3b4c3e450b25a789480ac53189ab92385174688e460b2cc.svg)\n\nUsing Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](images/41/4122fb4ef56aa99161b15bc25001ca728a6cf7dae36d5dac0aac9b03dc411685.svg)\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x -3y= 4\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186115124 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](images/50/50f13deaa03c2af30f511ef3d514e3dd2e118d81d9b121b436ff1a2f2497c303.png)\n\nUsing Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](images/e0/e02bb5004f792eea20216e64098bb924dbed15defb9330967d6ae5a144e067dc.png)\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x -3y= 4\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 13194139534277 17592186045417 false] [17592186115241 1038 #edb/ref 17592186417081 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186115242 1038 #edb/ref 17592186417082 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186115479 1050 720.0 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186116493 1064 "We can use Gaussian elimination to find the general solutions of systems with any number of equations and variables. For instance, consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1, \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\, & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4z=1 \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable $z.$ From the second equation, we get $y=-3z,$ and from the first equation, we obtain $x=1-4z.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-4z, \\\\ y=-3z, \\\\ z=z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534277 17592186045417 false] [17592186116493 1064 "We can use Gaussian elimination to find the general solutions of systems with any number of equations and variables. For instance, consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1, \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has the augmented matrix\n![](images/8a/8a8452587098eed9b697c3999c356359b949429f29ce16af2c81cf728be9480e.svg)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\, & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4z=1 \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable $z.$ From the second equation, we get $y=-3z,$ and from the first equation, we obtain $x=1-4z.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-4z, \\\\ y=-3z, \\\\ z=z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417069 1080 "k=2" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417069 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417069 1083 #uuid "0250b550-0b7c-5c05-b8f5-33da7345f93c" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417070 1080 "k=0" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417070 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417070 1083 #uuid "0e30254f-fef5-5030-ad74-62323657f390" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417071 1080 "k=\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417071 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417071 1083 #uuid "32810e7f-ad8d-5b1e-a7d2-839ff11f12a9" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417072 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2+z \\\\ -z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417072 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417072 1083 #uuid "46e61892-168f-50bc-9184-3087f0aa19c4" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417073 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}z \\\\ 2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417073 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417073 1083 #uuid "59f7a4dc-26a3-51be-9f66-57bb37e63b92" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417074 1080 "k=-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417074 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417074 1083 #uuid "5b0d5bd9-5c97-5445-afdc-58640864c07d" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417075 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2+z \\\\ z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417075 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417075 1083 #uuid "5e341f4d-4527-53f0-a549-17a212c07c94" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417076 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2+z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417076 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417076 1083 #uuid "86d4df82-dbcb-5384-b53a-8ca94675a39a" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417077 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2+z \\\\ -2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417077 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417077 1083 #uuid "b3937866-2599-550e-8d7d-230111af4c2c" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417078 1080 "k=\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417078 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417078 1083 #uuid "e23cbcca-7092-5855-aeeb-dd2de6061a27" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417069 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417070 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417071 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417074 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417078 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417079 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417079 1077 "selection" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417079 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417071 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417079 1079 #uuid "26b28742-5ee2-597a-8428-7062724625e9" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417080 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417072 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417080 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417073 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417080 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417075 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417080 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417076 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417080 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417077 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417080 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417080 1077 "selection" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417080 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417077 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417080 1079 #uuid "40f01e87-54e2-5dd2-9850-20313302577b" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417081 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417080 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417081 1069 "q-32220" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417081 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417081 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=2 \\\\  & y+2z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417081 1072 #uuid "32425960-ceab-536a-8061-1f2469974e99" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417081 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-z=2 \\\\  & y+2z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2+z \\\\ y=-2z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the latter can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+z \\\\ -2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417082 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417079 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417082 1069 "q-131730" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417082 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417082 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+2y=12 \\\\  & x+ky=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417082 1072 #uuid "6deb5ca1-ae5b-5721-895d-6efa8ac5fdfb" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true] [17592186417082 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2-3k & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+ky=4 \\\\  & (2-3k)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=\\frac{2}{3},$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+ky=4.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=\\frac{2}{3}.$" 13194139534277 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0250b550-0b7c-5c05-b8f5-33da7345f93c" 17592186417069 "answer-0e30254f-fef5-5030-ad74-62323657f390" 17592186417070 "answer-32810e7f-ad8d-5b1e-a7d2-839ff11f12a9" 17592186417071 "answer-46e61892-168f-50bc-9184-3087f0aa19c4" 17592186417072 "answer-59f7a4dc-26a3-51be-9f66-57bb37e63b92" 17592186417073 "answer-5b0d5bd9-5c97-5445-afdc-58640864c07d" 17592186417074 "answer-5e341f4d-4527-53f0-a549-17a212c07c94" 17592186417075 "answer-86d4df82-dbcb-5384-b53a-8ca94675a39a" 17592186417076 "answer-b3937866-2599-550e-8d7d-230111af4c2c" 17592186417077 "answer-e23cbcca-7092-5855-aeeb-dd2de6061a27" 17592186417078 "answer-field-26b28742-5ee2-597a-8428-7062724625e9" 17592186417079 "answer-field-40f01e87-54e2-5dd2-9850-20313302577b" 17592186417080 "question-32425960-ceab-536a-8061-1f2469974e99" 17592186417081 "question-6deb5ca1-ae5b-5721-895d-6efa8ac5fdfb" 17592186417082} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
